From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:45:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: depth export, shadow compare functions,
 tiled uploads

- Fragment shaders can write gl_FragDepth: export 61 (x), and
  SQ_PROGRAM_CNTL.PS_EXPORT_MODE gets bit 0 (3 instead of 2); with mode 2
  the export is ignored. Early Z is off for such shaders. cp_export leaves
  the depth export's mov alone (redirecting gl_FragCoord.z into it left
  the scheduler with nothing to issue).
- Shadow samplers honour GL_TEXTURE_COMPARE_FUNC: the compare function is
  a per-sampler fragment constant (IR2_SHADOW_CONST + sampler) holding
  less/equal/greater weights.
- Rectangle, 1D and depth/stencil resources are tiled, so CPU uploads of
  depth go through the conversion to the resolve's layout; the layout
  choice for Xenos follows fd2_tile_mode.
- Unsynchronized maps of tiled resources take the CPU (de)tiling path too.
  A fresh texture got UNSYNCHRONIZED from improve_transfer_map_usage and
  its data went in linear (glDrawPixels came out in 4-texel blocks).
- Depth conversion on the CPU only for the Z24 formats, not Z32_FLOAT.

